c230c8e2.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued November 2 at 3:47PM MST until November 3 at 3:45PM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"Flooding along the upper Conejos River continues.\n\n* WHAT...Flooding caused by rain and snowmelt is expected to\ncontinue.\n\n* WHERE...Western Conejos County in south central Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 345 PM MST Tuesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding along the upper Conejos River, for areas below\nPlatoro and downstream through Mogote, will continue into Tuesday.\nResidual impacts from flooding of smaller creeks, streams, and\nother low-lying and flood-prone locations may continue. Numerous\nroads remain closed due to flooding. Low-water crossings are\ninundated with water and may not be passable.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 343 PM MST, Rain and snowmelt from the previous 24 hours is\ncausing continued flooding.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMainly rural areas of Western Conejos County, from Platoro\ndownstream through Mogote.\n- http://www.water.noaa.gov","ends":"2026-11-03T15:45:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Conejos, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.aac508d852d6aadc0ffc543722b1bf27c1ab74d4.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.aac508d852d6aadc0ffc543722b1bf27c1ab74d4.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-03T04:40:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 030440 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 940 PM MST Mon Nov 2 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Strong north winds and showers/isolated t-storms on the plains into this evening, perhaps some snow showers along the Palmer Divide overnight. - Generally dry and breezy on Tue, strongest winds early in the day on the plains. - Weak trough will bring scattered show","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-02T08:09:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 020809 HWOP